    {'colophon': "|| atha caturtho'dhyāyaḥ ||", 'gloss': 'Here begins the fourth adhyāya.'},
    {'heading': '4.1 · The Naigama-kāṇḍa begins; jahā'},
    {'padas': ["ekārthamanekaśabdamityetaduktam | atha yānyanekārthānyekaśabdāni tānyato'nukramiṣyāmaḥ | anavagatasaṃskārāṃśca nigamān | tadaikapadikamityācakṣate |", 'jahā jaghānetyarthaḥ'], 'num': '|| 1 ||', 'gloss': 'The synonyms are done; now come words of one form with several senses, and words of the hymns whose formation is unclear: the "single words" (aikapadika). Jahā means "he struck".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.2 · Jahā, mamarya, nidhā'},
    {'padas': ['ko nu maryā amithitaḥ sakhā sakhāyamabravīt |', 'jahā ko asmadīṣate ||', "maryā iti manuṣyanāma | maryādābhidhānaṃ vā syāt | [ maryādā maryairādīyate ] maryādā maryādinorvibhāgaḥ | methatirākrośakarmā | apāpakaṃ jaghāna kamahaṃ jātu | ko'smadbhītaḥ palāyate |", 'nidhā pāśyā bhavati | yannidhīyate | pāśyā pāśasamūhaḥ | pāśaḥ pāśayateḥ | vipāśanāt'], 'num': '|| 2 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 8.45.37: what friend, unprovoked, has struck his friend? Maryā (men, or limits) and methati ("to revile"). Nidhā is a net, a mass of snares.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.3 · Nidhā; śitāma'},
    {'padas': ['vayaḥ suparṇā upa sedurindraṃ priyamedhā ṛṣayo nādhamānāḥ |', 'apa dhvāntamūrṇuhi pūrdhi cakṣurmumugdhyasmānnidhayeva baddhān ||', 'vayo verbahuvacanam | [ suparṇāḥ ] supatanā ādityaraśmaya upasedurindraṃ yācamānāḥ | aporṇuhyādhvastaṃ cakṣuḥ | cakṣuḥ khyātervā | caṣṭe vā | pūrdhi pūraya dehīti vā | muñcāsmān pāśairiva baddhān ||', 'pārśvataḥ śroṇitaḥ śitāmataḥ |', "pārśvaṃ parśumayamaṅgaṃ bhavati | parśuḥ spṛśateḥ | saṃspṛṣṭā pṛṣṭhadeśam | pṛṣṭhaṃ spṛśateḥ | saṃspṛṣṭamaṅgaiḥ | aṅgamaṅganāt | añcanādvā | śroṇiḥ śroṇatergaticalākarmaṇaḥ | śroṇiścalatīva gacchataḥ | doḥ śitāma bhavati | dordravateḥ | yoniḥ śitāmeti śākapūṇiḥ | viṣito bhavati | śyāmato yakṛtta iti taiṭīkiḥ | śyāmaṃ śyāyateḥ | yakṛd yathā kathā ca kṛtyate | śitimāṃsato medasta iti gālavaḥ | śitiḥ śyateḥ | māṃsaṃ mānanaṃ vā | mānasaṃ vā | mano'smintsīdatīti vā | medo medyateḥ"], 'num': '|| 3 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 10.73.11: the birds came to Indra asking to be freed as from a net; cakṣus. Śitāma in "from the sides, from the hips, from the śitāma": the arm, the womb, the liver or the fat, as various teachers hold.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.4 · Mehanā; damūnas'},
    {'padas': ['yadindra citra mehanāsti tvādātamadrivaḥ |', 'rādhastanno vidadvasa ubhayāhastyā bhara ||', 'yadindra [ citraṃ ] cāyanīyaṃ maṃhanīyaṃ dhanamasti | yanma iha nāstīti vā | trīṇi madhyamāni padāni | tvayā nastad dātavyam | adrivan | adrirādṛṇātyenena | api vātteḥ syāt |', 'te somādo | iti ha vijñāyate |', 'rādha iti dhananāma | rādhnuvantyanena | tannastvaṃ vittadhanobhābhyāṃ hastābhyāmāhara |', 'ubhau samubdhau bhavataḥ |', 'damūnā damamanā vā | dānamanā vā | dāntamanā vā | api vā dama iti gṛhanāma | tanmanā syāt | mano manoteḥ'], 'num': '|| 4 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.39.1: whatever bright wealth there is, Indra, bring it with both hands. Mehanā read as "what is with you" or as three words; adri, rādhas. Damūnas: "of tamed mind", "of giving mind", or "minded to the house".', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.5 · Damūnas, atithi, duroṇa; mūṣ'},
    {'padas': ['juṣṭo damūnā atithirduroṇa imaṃ no yajñamupa yāhi vidvān |', 'viśvā agne abhiyujo vihatyā śatrūyatāmā bharā bhojanāni ||', 'atithirabhyatito gṛhānbhavati | abhyeti tithiṣu parakulānīti vā | [ para ] gṛhāṇīti vā | duroṇa iti gṛhanāma | duravā bhavanti dustarpāḥ | imaṃ no yajñamupayāhi vidvān | sarvā agne abhiyujo vihatya śatrūyatāmābhara bhojanāni | vihatyānyeṣāṃ balāni śatrūṇāṃ bhavanādāhara bhojanānīti vā | dhanānīti vā |', "mūṣo mūṣikā ityarthaḥ | mūṣikāḥ punarmuṣṇāteḥ | mūṣo'pyetasmādeva"], 'num': '|| 5 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 5.4.5: Agni, the welcome house-friend and guest, come to our sacrifice. Atithi, duroṇa. Mūṣ, a mouse.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.6 · Trita in the well'},
    {'padas': ['saṃ mā tapantyabhitaḥ sapatnīriva parśavaḥ |', 'mūṣo na śiśnā vyadanti mādhyaḥ stotāraṃ te śatakrato', 'vittaṃ me asya rodasī ||', "santapanti māmabhitaḥ sapatnya ivemāḥ parśavaḥ kūpaparśavaḥ | mūṣikā ivāsnātāni sūtrāṇi vyadanti | svāṅgābhidhānaṃ vā syāt | śiśnāni vyadantīti vā | santapanti mādhyaḥ kāmāḥ | stotāraṃ te śatakrato [ vittaṃ me asya rodasī ] | jānītaṃ me'sya dyāvāpṛthivyāviti |", "tritaṃ kūpe'vahitametatsūktaṃ pratibabhau | tatra brahmetihāsamiśramṛṅmiśraṃ gāthāmiśraṃ bhavati | tritastīrṇatamo medhayā babhūva | api vā saṃkhyānāmaivābhipretaṃ syāt | ekato dvitastrita iti trayo babhūvuḥ"], 'num': '|| 6 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 1.105.8: the ribs torment me like rival wives, cares gnaw me as mice gnaw threads. The hymn came to Trita lying in a well; Trita, "the most outstanding in wisdom", or the third of three brothers.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.7 · Iṣira; the suffix -tana; jaṭhara'},
    {'padas': ['iṣireṇa te manasā sutasya bhakṣīmahi pitryasyeva rāyaḥ |', 'soma rājanpra ṇa āyūṃṣi tārīrahānīva sūryo vāsarāṇi ||', 'īṣaṇena vaiṣaṇena vārṣaṇena vā | te manasā sutasya bhakṣīmahi pitryasyeva dhanasya | pravardhaya ca na āyūṃṣi somarājan | ahānīva sūryo vāsarāṇi | vāsarāṇi vesarāṇi vivāsanāni gamanānīti vā |', 'kurutanetyanarthakā upajanā bhavanti | kartanahantanayātaneti |', 'jaṭharamudaraṃ bhavati | jagdhamasmindhriyate dhīyate vā'], 'num': '|| 7 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 8.48.7: with eager mind may we enjoy the soma as ancestral wealth. Vāsara. The meaningless additions in kartana, hantana, yātana. Jaṭhara, the belly.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.8 · Jaṭhara in use'},
    {'padas': ['marutvāṁ indra vṛṣabho raṇāya pibā somamanuṣvadhaṃ madāya |', 'ā siñcasva jaṭhare madhva ūrmiṃ tvaṃ rājāsi pradivaḥ sutānām ||', 'marutvānindra [ marudbhiḥ ] tadvān | vṛṣabho varṣitāpām | raṇāya ramaṇīyāya saṃgrāmāya | piba somam | anuṣvadhamanvannam | madāya madanīyāya jaitrāya | āsiñcasva jaṭhare madhuna ūrmim | madhu somamityaupamikaṃ mādyateḥ | idamapītaranmadhvetasmādeva | tvaṃ rājāsi pūrveṣvapyahaḥsu sutānām'], 'num': '|| 8 ||', 'gloss': 'Ṛgveda 3.47.1: drink the soma, Indra, with the Maruts; pour the wave of sweetness into your belly. Madhu.', 'prose': True},
    {'heading': '4.9 · Titau, the sieve'},
